==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**6 [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.
**1 [[Jackie Peng]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 88% HP:
**Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 3.33~13.33 seconds<sup>100f~400f</sup>.
**1 [[Jackie Peng]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Jackie Peng is stronger than [[Hippoe]] but can only hit one cat a time. The overall strategy for him is fairly similar to what you used against Hippoe, except now there are two of them, making [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|Bird Cat]] more important to have. Note that the two Pengs each spawn when the enemy base is at a slightly different percentage of HP, making it possible to face only one at a time by not playing too aggressively at the beginning.

Start the battle by upgrading your [[Worker Cat]] to max level, then spawn a few meatshields and an [[Axe Cat (Normal Cat)|Axe Cat]]. Save your money for Bird Cat and [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Cow Cat]]. When Jackie Peng spawns, keep spamming meatshields and spawn a few [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cats]]. When Bird Cat dies, immediately spawn another one.

Having the [[Energy Drink]] is recommended, as otherwise you may not be able to spawn your cats fast enough.

